course: dictionary
lesson: 4294
title: Words with -ish
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Greyish means a little bit grey. It is not fully grey, but it is close to it. Look at the ending: -ish means rather or somewhat, as in reddish, smallish and sevenish. So greyish is grey with a little extra softness on the end.
explain: «Frostbite makes skin white or greyish and numb, usually on fingers, toes, ears and nose.» Here greyish tells you the skin has a dull, pale shade that is not quite a normal colour. The words around it, numb and frostbite, show that something is wrong, so the colour is a warning sign.
explain: Greyish can also set a mood. «A greyish morning» sounds dull and cloudy, not bright and happy. Check any new word by swapping in a simpler one: if grey fits but is too strong, greyish is the softer, less exact version.
fact: Greyish means a little bit grey, or rather grey.
fact: The ending -ish means rather or somewhat: reddish, smallish, sevenish.
fact: Of hair, sky or light, greyish means starting to look grey.
fact: «Greyish-blue» describes a colour that is mostly blue with a touch of grey.
fact: The American spelling is grayish, with the same meaning.
exercise: «Dogs see blue and yellow well, but red and green look greyish to them.» What does greyish mean here? | *A little bit grey | Bright and shiny | Very loud | Wet and cold
exercise: What does the ending -ish mean in greyish? | Under or below | Not at all | Very or extremely | *Rather or somewhat
exercise: Which word means rather red? | red-hot | *reddish | redness | redden
test: «A greyish morning» sets what kind of mood? | Bright and sunny | Noisy and busy | *Dull and cloudy | Hot and sticky
test: What does «smallish» mean? | Not small at all | Very big | *Rather small | Smaller than a mouse
exam: Read this: «Frostbite makes skin white or greyish.» What does greyish mean? | Shiny and wet | Bright red | Very grey | *A little bit grey
